.TH CCCLONE 1 "2026-07-17" "codecommit-utils" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ccclone \- clone an AWS CodeCommit repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ccclone
.I repository\-name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ccclone
is
.BR "git clone" (1)
for CodeCommit: it clones the named repository over HTTPS into the current
directory. The clone URL is read from the repository metadata, so only the
repository name is needed.
.PP
It is a thin wrapper around
.BR cch (1),
which holds the implementation:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ccclone \fIrepository\-name\fR    is  cch repo clone \fIrepository\-name\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Both spellings are fully supported.
.BR cch (1)
is the recommended entry point for new work.
.PP
Use
.BR cclist (1)
or
.B cch repo list
to see the available repository names. When zsh completions are enabled,
completion on the repository name lists the repositories for the current AWS
profile.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AWS_PROFILE
The AWS profile whose credentials and region are used, as for the AWS CLI.
.TP
.B AWS_REGION
The AWS region to operate in, as for the AWS CLI.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 on success, and 1 when no repository name is supplied. Failures
reported by the AWS CLI or by
.BR git (1)
propagate their own exit status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cch (1),
.BR cclist (1),
.BR ccinit (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR aws (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/easytocloud/codecommit\-utils/issues .
